prompt:
Implement a robot dance choreographer using Three.js. Set animation keyframes through a timeline.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/RobotExpressive.glb;
(2) Center the model and list the names of all available animation clips;

[Timeline System]
(3) A timeline bar at the bottom (DOM or canvas, total duration 10 seconds, id="timeline");
(4) Clicking a position on the timeline adds a "keyframe" marker;
(5) A menu opens for each keyframe to select the animation clip to play;
(6) During playback, automatically switch animations upon reaching a keyframe (using a crossFadeTo transition);

[Playback Controls]
(7) Play/Pause button (id="playBtn");
(8) Speed control slider (id="speedSlider", range 0.5-2);
(9) Loop playback (return to 0 seconds after reaching 10 seconds);

[Beat Indicator]
(10) BPM slider (id="bpmSlider", range 60-180, default 120);
(11) A pulsing circle flashes according to the BPM (CSS or canvas);

[HUD Display]
(12) HUD in the upper-left corner:
  - Current time (id="currentTime")
  - Playback state (id="playState")
  - Number of keyframes (id="keyframeCount")
  - BPM value (id="bpmValue")

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - modelLoaded: boolean
  - currentTime: number (0-10 seconds)
  - isPlaying: boolean
  - keyframeCount: number
  - bpm: number
  - currentAnim: string (name of the animation currently playing)
  - speed: number

Output a standalone HTML file.
